/*****************************************************************************
    colorList -- the colours as a poured list (Tony and Clay, 2026-11-22; derived rows since SEQ 742).
    Definitions only. Fire it with  Start(); show(colorList);
    The form says only what to pour: clRows holds no template row, so pour works out each row from
    what a member IS -- a colour here: its name, a swatch printing its value in contrast text, and
    its words from dESCRIPTIONs. The form names no colour and no font of its own: only placeholders,
    resolved through the look (IncantForms/Controls/styles).
*****************************************************************************/
/*  The words for each colour, in dESCRIPTIONs, keyed by the colour's own name, as a field's
    description is keyed by the field's name (Tony, 2026-11-22: no registry of their own).
    cOLOr is on the search list while these are read, and black="..." still makes dESCRIPTIONs' own black:
    a definition whose name is found in another registry gets its own entry (SEQ 744; until then this file
    reset the search list around the define, or cOLOr's black was overwritten).
    genLadder/describedTwice.sh names any name described in two places.  */
register(dESCRIPTIONs);
define
    black="the darkest; default text";
    blue="a strong mid blue";
    darkBrown="a deep brown";
    darkerGray="a cool mid grey";
    gray="a light grey";
    green="a strong green";
    lightBlue="a very pale blue";
    lightGreen="a soft green; the tab fill";
    paleGray="the palest grey";
    radialGreen="lightGreen's value, old name";
    red="strong red; the accent";
    saberBrown="a sand brown";
    wall="pale yellow; old page colour";
    white="white; the page fill";
    ;
register(FORMs);
define
    colorList window x=0 y=0 width=490 height=fit margin=12 down fill:=pageFill font:=bodyFont title="Colors"
        clTitle="Colors" text height=40 font:=headingFont align=center valign=center bottomBorder;
        clRows down="*" pour:=cOLOr gap=4;
    ;
bail();

HOW IT WORKS (pour stage 2, SEQ 742; incant/utilities, pourPlan):
    pour:=cOLOr on a down="*" field with no row of its own: one row a member of cOLOr, in order, three cells.
    margin=12 stands the content 12 points in; gap=4 puts 4 points between rows; height=fit makes the window as tall
    as its rows need (capped at the page, 792, until a window knows its display).
    A written template row under clRows is the override (stage 1): pour then copies that row, and each stands for the
    member under its copy -- {each}, {each.taG}, fill:=each, {dESCRIPTIONs.each}. incant/pop/pourT keeps one.
    Poured from fONTs or sTYLEs the same field shows sample text in each font, or with each style.
ISSUES:
- Six descriptions are the design pass's short ones (tester's colorListHand, 2026-11-22); Clod shortened the other eight to match.
